38.jpg\"]},\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-16T11:05:44.663Z\",\"variations\":[{\"id\":\"f51342fd-42be-4be4-824e-59c30fa46767\",\"creativeVersionId\":\"45299907-36dc-490e-9ca6-d6e765a799bb\",\"variationType\":\"size\",\"variationKey\":\"original\",\"width\":null,\"height\":null,\"aspectRatio\":null,\"platform\":null,\"isPrimary\":true,\"storageKey\":null,\"assetUrl\":null,\"thumbnailUrl\":null,\"mimeType\":null,\"downloadCount\":0,\"status\":\"generating\",\"metadata\":{\"brief\":\"Using the AIDA (Attention-Interest-Desire-Action) framework, this lifestyle-first discovery ad addresses the morning struggle of waking up depleted. The visual hero is the beautiful coral-red and deep-burgundy canister sitting elegantly on a marble countertop in a bright, sun-drenched kitchen, bathed in warm morning light next to a clean glass of water and a single transparent capsule. This inviting, aspirational scene serves as a warm aesthetic pattern interrupt that visualizes a seamless, elevated morning ritual. The headline, \\\"Wake up feeling actually awake.\\\", is written in the modern, friendly sans-serif Circular Std in Premium Black, occupying less than 15% of the frame. The soft CTA reads \\\"see how it works\\\" inside a minimal, thin black-bordered pill-shaped tag. To keep this ad on-brand, keep the photography extremely airy and optimistic, use the soft Wellness Cream background tone, and ensure the vibrant color-blocked canister pops dynamically against the warm neutral kitchen environment to instantly communicate daily wellness.\",\"prompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Using the AIDA (Attention-Interest-Desire-Action) framework, this lifestyle-first discovery ad addresses the morning struggle of waking up depleted. The visual hero is the beautiful coral-red and deep-burgundy canister sitting elegantly on a marble countertop in a bright, sun-drenched kitchen, bathed in warm morning light next to a clean glass of water and a single transparent capsule. This inviting, aspirational scene serves as a warm aesthetic pattern interrupt that visualizes a seamless, elevated morning ritual. The headline, \\\"Wake up feeling actually awake.\\\", is written in the modern, friendly sans-serif Circular Std in Premium Black, occupying less than 15% of the frame. The soft CTA reads \\\"see how it works\\\" inside a minimal, thin black-bordered pill-shaped tag. To keep this ad on-brand, keep the photography extremely airy and optimistic, use the soft Wellness Cream background tone, and ensure the vibrant color-blocked canister pops dynamically against the warm neutral kitchen environment to instantly communicate daily wellness.\\n\\nProduct appearance: The product consists of a tall, matte-finished cylindrical canister and an accompanying dietary supplement capsule. The canister features a two-tone color-blocked design, with the top third in a vibrant coral-red and the bottom two-thirds in a deep burgundy-maroon. At the top of the coral-red section is a white circular logo reading \\\"WELLBEING NUTRITION\\\" wrapped around a stylized central \\\"W\\\", with a small green-and-white vegetarian symbol to its right. Spanning the color transition is the word \\\"slow\\\" in a large, lowercase, white sans-serif typeface, situated above the stacked white capital text \\\"LIPOSOMAL\\\" and \\\"IRON COMPLEX\\\". Below the text, the maroon section displays an angled graphic of a clear capsule filled with pink micro-pellets, decorated with a small circular \\\"2 SALTS\\\" badge, followed by explanatory white text detailing the ingredients and health benefits. Near the bottom, a physical horizontal seam defines the canister's base, which features two white icons for \\\"SUSTAINED RELEASE\\\" and \\\"2in1 NUTRI-SCIENCE\\\", the quantity \\\"60 N CAPSULES\\\" inside a pill-shaped border, and \\\"HEALTH SUPPLEMENT FOR ADULTS\\\" at the bottom edge. Beside the canister stands a physical, three-dimensional capsule with a completely transparent, glossy outer shell, revealing an interior packed tightly with hundreds of uniform, tiny, spherical micro-pellets in a soft, dusty-pink hue.\\n\\nUse the product appearance text only as a private visual reference for accurately drawing the product. Do not print, quote, paraphrase, label, or turn any of that description into ad copy. Treat orientation-specific details carefully: show front-only details only when the product front is visible; if the brief shows the back, side, top, or an angled view where those details would not be visible, omit them instead of moving them onto the wrong face.\\n\\nThe attached product photos show the real product — reproduce it faithfully.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the supporting message, then the CTA.\\n- Keep strong figure/ground contrast. If text sits over imagery, place a scrim or\\n  overlay behind it so it stays fully legible.\\n- Place the focal subject on a rule-of-thirds line; leave generous whitespace and\\n  avoid clutter.\\n- Use a limited palette anchored to the brand colors (~60-30-10), reserving one\\n  accent color for the call to action.\\n- Keep 20% space all around the creative for the ad to look cleaner\\n- Group and align elements cleanly (Gestalt); use at most two type styles.\",\"source\":\"campaign-creatives\",\"language\":\"English\",\"lastError\":null,\"imageModel\":\"openai/gpt-image-2:100\",\"hasNSFWRisk\":false,\"imagePrompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Using the AIDA (Attention-Interest-Desire-Action) framework, this lifestyle-first discovery ad addresses the morning struggle of waking up depleted. The visual hero is the beautiful coral-red and deep-burgundy canister sitting elegantly on a marble countertop in a bright, sun-drenched kitchen, bathed in warm morning light nex