 At the top of the coral-red section is a white circular logo reading \\\"WELLBEING NUTRITION\\\" wrapped around a stylized central \\\"W\\\", with a small green-and-white vegetarian symbol to its right. Spanning the color transition is the word \\\"slow\\\" in a large, lowercase, white sans-serif typeface, situated above the stacked white capital text \\\"LIPOSOMAL\\\" and \\\"IRON COMPLEX\\\". Below the text, the maroon section displays an angled graphic of a clear capsule filled with pink micro-pellets, decorated with a small circular \\\"2 SALTS\\\" badge, followed by explanatory white text detailing the ingredients and health benefits. Near the bottom, a physical horizontal seam defines the canister's base, which features two white icons for \\\"SUSTAINED RELEASE\\\" and \\\"2in1 NUTRI-SCIENCE\\\", the quantity \\\"60 N CAPSULES\\\" inside a pill-shaped border, and \\\"HEALTH SUPPLEMENT FOR ADULTS\\\" at the bottom edge. Beside the canister stands a physical, three-dimensional capsule with a completely transparent, glossy outer shell, revealing an interior packed tightly with hundreds of uniform, tiny, spherical micro-pellets in a soft, dusty-pink hue.\\n\\nUse the product appearance text only as a private visual reference for accurately drawing the product. Do not print, quote, paraphrase, label, or turn any of that description into ad copy. Treat orientation-specific details carefully: show front-only details only when the product front is visible; if the brief shows the back, side, top, or an angled view where those details would not be visible, omit them instead of moving them onto the wrong face.\\n\\nThe attached product photos show the real product — reproduce it faithfully.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then 