ows the back, side, top, or an angled view where those details would not be visible, omit them instead of moving them onto the wrong face.\\n\\nThe attached product photos show the real product — reproduce it faithfully.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the supporting message, then the CTA.\\n- Keep strong figure/ground contrast. If text sits over imagery, place a scrim or\\n  overlay behind it so it stays fully legible.\\n- Place the focal subject on a rule-of-thirds line; leave generous whitespace and\\n  avoid clutter.\\n- Use a limited palette anchored to the brand colors (~60-30-10), reserving one\\n  accent color for the call to action.\\n- Keep 20% space all around the creative for the ad to look cleaner\\n- Group and align elements cleanly (Gestalt); use at most two type styles.\",\"source\":\"campaign-creatives\",\"language\":\"English\",\"lastError\":null,\"imageModel\":\"openai/gpt-image-2:100\",\"hasNSFWRisk\":false,\"imagePrompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Using the AIDA (Attention-Interest-Desire-Action) framework, this lifestyle-first discovery ad addresses the morning struggle of waking up depleted. The visual hero is the beautiful coral-red and deep-burgundy canister sitting elegantly on a marble countertop in a bright, sun-drenched kitchen, bathed in warm morning light next to a clean glass of water and a single transparent capsule. This inviting, aspirational scene serves as a warm aesthetic pattern interrupt that visualizes a seamless, elevated morning ritual. The headline, \\\"Wake up feeling actually awake.\\\", is written in the modern, friendly sans-serif Circular Std in Premium Black, occupying less than 15% of the frame. The soft CTA reads \\\"see how it works\\\" inside a minimal, thin b