cylindrical canister and an accompanying dietary supplement capsule. The canister features a two-tone color-blocked design, with the top third in a vibrant coral-red and the bottom two-thirds in a deep burgundy-maroon. At the top of the coral-red section is a white circular logo reading \\\"WELLBEING NUTRITION\\\" wrapped around a stylized central \\\"W\\\", with a small green-and-white vegetarian symbol to its right. Spanning the color transition is the word \\\"slow\\\" in a large, lowercase, white sans-serif typeface, situated above the stacked white capital text \\\"LIPOSOMAL\\\" and \\\"IRON COMPLEX\\\". Below the text, the maroon section displays an angled graphic of a clear capsule filled with pink micro-pellets, decorated with a small circular \\\"2 SALTS\\\" badge, followed by explanatory white text detailing the ingredients and health benefits. Near the bottom, a physical horizontal seam defines the canister's base, which features two white icons for \\\"SUSTAINED RELEASE\\\" and \\\"2in1 NUTRI-SCIENCE\\\", the quantity \\\"60 N CAPSULES\\\" inside a pill-shaped border, and \\\"HEALTH SUPPLEMENT FOR ADULTS\\\" at the bottom edge. Beside the canister stands a physical, three-dimensional capsule with a completely transparent, glossy outer shell, revealing an interior packed tightly with hundreds of uniform, tiny, spherical micro-pellets in a soft, dusty-pink hue.\\n\\nUse the product appearance text only as a private visual reference for accurately drawing the product. Do not print, quote, paraphrase, label, or turn any of that description into ad copy. Treat orientation-specific details carefully: show front-only details only when the product front is visible; if the brief shows the back, side, top, or an angled view where those details would not be visible, omit them instead of moving them onto the wrong face.\\n\\nThe attached product photos show the real product — reproduce it faithfully.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the supporting message, then the CTA.\\n- Keep strong figure/ground contrast. If text sits over imagery, place a scrim or\\n  overlay behind it so it stays fully legible.\\n- Place the focal subject on a rule-of-thirds line; leave generous whitespace and\\n  avoid clutter.\\n- Use a limited palette anchored to the brand colors (~60-30-10), reserving one\\n  accent color for the call to action.\\n- Keep 20% space all around the creative for the ad to look cleaner\\n- Group and align elements cleanly (Gestalt); use at most two type styles.\",\"source\":\"campaign-creatives\",\"language\":\"English\",\"lastError\":null,\"imageModel\":\"openai/gpt-image-2:100\",\"hasNSFWRisk\":false,\"imagePrompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Using the BAB (Before-After-Bridge) framework, this product-led discovery ad targets health-conscious individuals who struggle with the stomach cramps and poor absorption of standard iron supplements. The visual hero is a hyper-detailed, macro-photographic close-up of the single transparent capsule, showcasing the hundreds of uniform, dusty-pink micro-pellets packed tightly inside, suspended weightlessly over a clinical Mist Gray background with a soft, diagonal white gradient. This clean, high-tech aesthetic acts as a pattern interrupt against typical cluttered health ads, positioning the supplement as a premium, science-backed upgrade. The minimalist headline, \\\"Iron absorption, minus stomach pain.\\\", is set in the sophisticated Tenor Sans typeface to convey an elegant, editorial feel. The soft CTA is a clean \\\"explore the collection\\\" link in bold Outfit typeface at the bottom. To keep this ad on-brand, maintain an ultra-clean, clinical layout with generous negative space, use the vibrant Brand Orange for subtle accent 