e warm, natural Sand Beige side, use the clean, clinical look of the Outfit typeface for supporting details, and showcase the capsule's pink micro-pellets in sharp, glossy high-resolution.\",\"prompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Using the PAS (Problem-Agitation-Solution) framework, this discovery ad targets people suffering from chronic iron-deficiency fatigue. The visual layout is a stark, split-screen contrast: the left half is a dim, cool-toned photograph of a woman slumped at her work desk at 2:00 PM, overwhelmed by brain fog and surrounded by three empty coffee mugs; the right half is a clean, warm Sand Beige block featuring a 3D render of the transparent capsule filled with dusty-pink micro-pellets. This layout creates an instant pattern interrupt in the feed by highlighting the familiar frustration of caffeine-resistant afternoon fatigue. The bold headline, \\\"Tired of feeling constantly tired?\\\", is styled in the premium, geometric sans-serif Circular Std in Premium Black, occupying under 10% of the overall layout. The soft CTA at the bottom reads \\\"learn more\\\" in a sharp, rectangular pill-shaped button with a 0px border radius using the primary brand orange to draw the eye. To keep the ad on-brand, ensure the lifestyle side transitions smoothly to the warm, natural Sand Beige side, use the clean, clinical look of the Outfit typeface for supporting details, and showcase the capsule's pink micro-pellets in sharp, glossy high-resolution.\\n\\nProduct appearance: The product consists of a tall, matte-finished cylindrical canister and an accompanying dietary supplement capsule. The canister features a two-tone color-blocked design, with the top third in a vibrant coral-red and the bottom two-thirds in a deep burgundy-maroon. At the top of the coral-red section is a white circular logo reading \\\"WELLBEING NUTRITION\\\" wrapped around a stylized central \\\"W\\\", with a small green-and-white vegetarian symbol to its right. Spanning the color transi